WEBVTT

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Welcome. Today we walk through the GROW model — Goal, Reality, Options, Will — as a practical structure for every coaching conversation.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Start with Goal. Ask what the coachee wants from this session and from the longer journey. How will they know they have succeeded? A vague wish is not a goal until it is specific and owned by them.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Reality comes next. Explore what is happening now without rushing to fix it. What have they tried? What obstacles are real versus assumed? The coach's job is to raise awareness, not to supply answers.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Options is the creative stage. Generate many possibilities before judging any of them. Say "What else?" until the list feels complete. If they say they have no options, ask what they would do if a friend faced the same situation.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:55.000
Will is commitment. Which option will they take? By when? What might get in the way, and how will they handle it? End with a concrete next step they choose themselves — that is where performance coaching creates accountability.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:18.000
Technique: when a client keeps revisiting the problem, gently return them to the stage you are in. "We agreed the goal is X — let's stay with Reality for a moment before we jump to solutions."
